nodecode-tripwire is a rewrite of percyhendrux123-prog's percyhendrux123-prog/hermes-tripwire:

  https://github.com/percyhendrux123-prog/hermes-tripwire
  commit 904a4f559808c57152ebb666cd0ab7d863220b49
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Deploy Axiom (LICENSE)

The original is a plugin for another agent harness: it listens for a blocked
tool call and for a denied approval, writes one line about each to a shared
JSON-lines file, and ships a small scheduled script that reads the new lines
and prints one alert. This rewrite keeps that record and reimplements it in
Common Lisp against Nodecode's own seams: one :TOOL point hook records what a
refused call answered, `/tripwire` and the `tripwire_digest` tool are the
digest the scheduled script used to print, and the original's `TEST_BLOCK`
switch file (which blocked one tool in one profile) became the declared
`drill_tool` setting, so the alarm can still be proved end to end. The
approval half is read off the refusal text an approval card produces, because
Nodecode asks the question through the guard cell's own path rather than a
separate approval hook; the count-every-event bookkeeping (a byte offset, a
cross-process file lock) is a line count and one in-process lock, since one
Nodecode process owns a home. The original's fields, its 120-character
reason, its never-store-the-arguments rule and its fail-open posture are kept.
